5 1.04 2.31<BR>            1 ord1-sjc1-oc3.ord1.above.net 0% 60 60 61.74 75.51 368.10<BR>            2 bx3-chicago23-pos8-0-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 61.84 107.48<BR>502.02<BR>            3 bx2-chicago23-pos7-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 61.72 63.30<BR>67.06<BR>            4 core2-chicago23-pos10-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 61.69 63.32<BR>66.40<BR>            5 core1-toronto12-pos3-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 73.38 74.85<BR>80.14<BR>            6 core2-vancouver-pos3-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 130.24<BR>131.55 136.21<BR>            7 dis1-regina-pos8-1-0.in.bellnexxia.net 0% 60 60 169.69 186.06<BR>444.23<BR>            8 sasktel-gw.dis1-regina-atm12-0-0-33.in.bellnexxia.net 15% 51<BR>60 251.58 332.87 1809.25<BR>            9 142.165.18.228 10% 54 60 248.54 273.25 427.14<BR>            10 hss-dslam-62-36.sk.sympatico.ca 5% 57 60 268.83 285.82 314.59<BR>            Fail:<P>Yup, sure enough, I did the line quality test and things go fine until they hit my local servers, and then I start to get bad packet loss. Check out the bottom 3 servers (Sasktel and Sympatico ones) on the East and West coast servers, the packetloss ranges from 4% to 15%. Pretty brutal, I think I might have to switch back to my old internet service provider.||||reg||2
Z||000008||FieroSTETZ||01-13-2001||01:16 PM||||1430 kb/sec down, 30kb/sec up (capped in my area) its all about the registry, baby... go to <A HREF="http://www.speedguide.net-" TARGET=_blank>www.speedguide.net-</A>  also, for downloading, there is a program called "downoad accelerator" which will open as many as 7 seperate connections to one files... hauls butt||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||01-13-2001||01:42 PM||||This has all been an interesting little thread. I had previously installed a thing called @Home Accelerator. After looking at that last link that was listed I see that @Home doesn't support this program and as a matter of fact, it can hurt performance instead of help it.<P>I downloaded a tweak from that page that is specifically written for Windows ME systems using broadband connections. I installed the tweak, restarted and ran the speed test at dslreports.com again. Here are my results...<P>** Speed 1920(down)/109(up) kbps **<BR>(At least 38 times faster than a 56k modem)<P>(See 'before' results in post above.)<P>Before doing this I was 12 times faster than a 56k modem. This goes to show that not all tweaks are a good thing.<P>Thanks for the thread and the links!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000010||loafer87gt||01-13-2001||07:32 PM||||Yes! I finally got my internet connection working better. I downloade the registry tweaks from <A HREF="http://cable-dsl.home.att.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://cable-dsl.home.att.net/</A>  and things seemed to improve a lot. My old download speeds were 190 dl/ 53 ul. Now I am getting 1143 dl/ 120 ul. For you guys doing the tests, be sure to clear out your cache before doing the tests. I did a couple of test one after another and was getting really high (4000+) speeds, until I cleaned my cache out and then they went back to normal. I also did the line quality test over <A HREF="http://www.dslreports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dslreports.com</A>  and found that the weak link is one of the network routers in town here. It shows that the server is consitently suffering from about 15% packet loss. That would explain all the lag and packetloss I get when trying to play some Quake or Tribes. Anyways, thanks for the help guys!||||reg||10
